              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Creditors can pursue directors individually for repayment, which may impact personal finances and credit ratings."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              6,
              1,
              7,
              10,
              4,
              13,
              3,
              5,
              14,
              15,
              11,
              12,
              16
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2324,
              "end_index": 2360,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Wrongful trading is a civil offence."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              6,
              7,
              13,
              3
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2549,
              "end_index": 2721,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Directors found guilty of fraudulent trading can face severe penalties, including personal liability for company debts, fines, and even a prison sentence of up to 10 years."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              10,
              5,
              11
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2722,
              "end_index": 3004,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Overdrawn Director's Loan Account:** If a director has taken more money from the company than they are entitled to (e.g., salary, dividends), creating an overdrawn director's loan account, this becomes an asset of the company in liquidation and must be repaid by the director."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              6
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3146,
              "end_index": 3311,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Breaches such as misusing company assets, paying unlawful dividends, or making preferential payments to certain creditors over others can lead to personal liability."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              6
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3312,
              "end_index": 3466,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Failure to Maintain Proper Accounting Records:** Serious failures in record-keeping can also be a ground for personal liability or disqualification."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              5
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3711,
              "end_index": 3913,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Personal Liability Notices (PLNs) can also be issued for unpaid PAYE, National Insurance, or Construction Industry Scheme deductions if the director intentionally or recklessly failed to ensure payment."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              1,
              17,
              18,
              19,
              20,
              21
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4070,
              "end_index": 4181,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "This can lead to disqualification proceedings under the **Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 (CDDA)**."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              6,
              1,
              7,
              17,
              18,
              19,
              20,
              21,
              5,
              15,
              11
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4183,
              "end_index": 4422,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Disqualification Period:** Directors can be disqualified from acting as a company director (or being involved in its formation, promotion, or management) for a period of **2 to 15 years**, depending on the severity of the misconduct."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              17,
              19,
              20
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4639,
              "end_index": 4801,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Breaching a disqualification order can result in criminal penalties (including imprisonment) and personal liability for company debts incurred during that period."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              17
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4802,
              "end_index": 5029,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Compensation Orders:** The Insolvency Service can also seek compensation orders under Section 15A of the CDDA, requiring a disqualified director to pay compensation for losses to creditors resulting from their misconduct."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              21
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5030,
              "end_index": 5214,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Timeline:** Disqualification proceedings under the CDDA usually must be commenced against the director within **three years** of the date of the formal insolvency of the company."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              6,
              18,
              22
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5677,
              "end_index": 5796,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Exceptions apply, such as obtaining court permission or purchasing the business from the liquidator with proper notice."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              7
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5827,
              "end_index": 6008,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Redundancy:** If directors were employees of the company and paid via PAYE, they may be able to claim redundancy payments from the government, provided they meet the criteria."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              0
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 6009,
              "end_index": 6183,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Public Record:** The director's name will be listed in public records related to the insolvency, which may affect their ability to secure future directorships or loans."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              10
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 6184,
              "end_index": 6406,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Personal Credit Rating:** Generally, a company liquidation does not directly impact a director's personal credit rating unless personal guarantees are called upon or personal insolvency (e.g., bankruptcy) is pursued."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              7,
              8,
              23,
              10,
              3,
              5
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 6408,
              "end_index": 6579,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "To mitigate these risks, it is crucial for directors to seek professional advice from a licensed insolvency practitioner as soon as their company faces financial distress."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              8,
              10
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 6580,
              "end_index": 6702,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Early action and adherence to legal responsibilities are key to ensuring the best possible outcome for directors in a CVL."
            }
          }
        ],
